" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135764022.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/govt-mulls-special-session-to-pass-womens-quota-amendment-bill-report/articleshow/135764022.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/govt-mulls-special-session-to-pass-womens-quota-amendment-bill-report/articleshow/135764022.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-12T15:40:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135764762,imgsize-262100.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[People free to protest against Congress: Priyanka Gandhi on police action against Kerala protesters]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/people-free-to-protest-against-congress-priyanka-gandhi-on-police-action-against-kerala-protesters/articleshow/135764208.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135764208.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/people-free-to-protest-against-congress-priyanka-gandhi-on-police-action-against-kerala-protesters/articleshow/135764208.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/people-free-to-protest-against-congress-priyanka-gandhi-on-police-action-against-kerala-protesters/articleshow/135764208.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-12T15:32:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135764396,imgsize-100018.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Sad day for democracy': Bombay HC warns against criminalising constitutional right to protest]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sad-day-for-democracy-bombay-hc-warns-against-criminalising-constitutional-right-to-protest/articleshow/135764160.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135764160.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Bombay high court has overturned an FIR against Nishkarsh Nimgade, highlighting the fundamental constitutional right to peaceful assembly during his protest over poor road conditions in Chandrapur district. The court recognised this right as vital to the democratic fabric and stated that criminal charges shouldn't stifle non-violent protests. Sparked by an accident linked to these conditions, the court condemned the prosecution of Nimgade as a misuse of legal resources.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sad-day-for-democracy-bombay-hc-warns-against-criminalising-constitutional-right-to-protest/articleshow/135764160.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sad-day-for-democracy-bombay-hc-warns-against-criminalising-constitutional-right-to-protest/articleshow/135764160.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-12T15:31:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135764210,imgsize-2027676.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[After NEET row, NTA invites retired defence personnel to monitor exams]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/after-neet-row-nta-invites-retired-defence-personnel-to-monitor-exams/articleshow/135763629.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135763629.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/after-neet-row-nta-invites-retired-defence-personnel-to-monitor-exams/articleshow/135763629.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/after-neet-row-nta-invites-retired-defence-personnel-to-monitor-exams/articleshow/135763629.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-12T15:10:45+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Priyanka Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135763629,imgsize-62322.cms"/></item></channel></rss>